/-!
# The first higher direct image of the structure sheaf is of finite type

For a proper morphism `f : X ⟶ Y` all of whose fibres have dimension at most one, `R¹ f_* 𝒪_X`
is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_Y`-module of finite type: the finite-type clause of [Stacks, Tag 0EX4] in
degree `d = 1` for the structure sheaf, over an arbitrary base. This is the statement
`FirstDirectImageFiniteTypeOfFibreDimensionOne` of `GloballyGeneratedVanishing.lean`, which the
vanishing statements of [Stacks, Tags 0E7F, 0E7G, 0E7H] consume.

## The argument

It is the source's: the question is local on `Y`, so `Y` is affine and one must show that
`H¹(X, 𝒪_X)` is a finite `Γ(Y, 𝒪_Y)`-module.

* `f` factors as a closed immersion `X ⟶ Z` followed by a proper morphism `Z ⟶ Y` of finite
  presentation whose fibres still have dimension at most one ([Stacks, Tags 09ZR, 05M6]). As
  `H²` of quasi-coherent modules on `Z` vanishes ([Stacks, Tag 0E7D]), `H¹(Z, 𝒪_Z)` surjects onto
  `H¹(Z, k_* 𝒪_X) = H¹(X, 𝒪_X)` (`moduleFinite_cohomologyOne_of_isClosedImmersion`).
* `Z ⟶ Y` is the base change of a proper morphism with one-dimensional fibres onto an affine
  Noetherian scheme ([Stacks, Tags 01ZM, 081F, 05M5]), whose `H¹(𝒪)` is finite by
  [Stacks, Tag 02O6].
* Finiteness of `H¹(𝒪)` survives an affine base change `Spec B ⟶ Spec R`
  (`moduleFinite_cohomologyOne_baseChange_of_isAffine`). This is where the top-degree base change
  [Stacks, Tag 0EX3] (b) enters, in the following elementwise form, which needs no comparison map
  of sheaves: `g'_* 𝒪_P` is generated by the global sections `b ∈ B`
  (`baseChangeGeneratingSections`, from [Stacks, Tag 02KG]); vanishing of `H²` makes `H¹` of the
  generating epimorphism surjective, and `H¹` commutes with direct sums ([Stacks, Tag 01FF]), so
  every class of `H¹(P, 𝒪_P) = H¹(Z, g'_* 𝒪_P)` ([Stacks, Tag 089W]) is a `B`-combination of
  pullbacks of classes of `H¹(Z, 𝒪_Z)`.

## Main results

* `firstDirectImageFiniteTypeOfFibreDimensionOne`: the finite-type clause.
* `moduleFinite_cohomologyOne_of_isAffine`: its affine form.
* `moduleFinite_cohomologyOne_baseChange_of_isAffine`: finiteness of `H¹(𝒪)` after an affine base
  change.
* `mem_iSup_range_rightDerived_one_of_generatingSections`: `H¹` of a globally generated module is
  spanned by the images of `H¹(𝒪)`, when `H²` vanishes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EX4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EX4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0EX3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0EX3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0E7D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0E7D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 089W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089W)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02KG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02KG)
-/

